import JournalArt from './JournalArt.astro';
---
<figure class="memory-flow"><figcaption>For each request, Lore composes context from eligible material.</figcaption><ul class="memory-inputs"><li><strong>Recent conversation</strong><span>The current work, kept in detail</span></li><li><strong>Distilled context</strong><span>Compressed observations from older work</span></li><li><strong>Relevant knowledge</strong><span>Project rules selected for this task</span></li></ul><div class="memory-flow-target"><JournalArt name="satchel" size={64} /><div><strong>Current request</strong><p>Material supplied to the agent within its scope and context budget.</p></div></div><p class="memory-flow-note">Stored history remains searchable through recall. Saving a conversation does not mean sending all of it on every request.</p></figure>
<dl class="memory-definitions"><div><dt>Stored conversation</dt><dd>Original messages and tool results, available for later search. Inspect them in <strong>Sessions</strong>.</dd></div><div><dt>Distilled context</dt><dd>Compressed observations from older work. Inspect session context and distillation views.</dd></div><div><dt>Project knowledge</dt><dd>Durable decisions, patterns and lessons. Review them in <strong>Knowledge</strong> and <code>.lore.md</code>.</dd></div><div><dt>Current context</dt><dd>The material composed for a particular request. Inspect session context where recorded.</dd></div></dl>
